            <div xml:id="d661">

                <pb facs="0809" n="713" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg713"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/8939</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Shidehara</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic">August 22,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have just received from
                    Tokio a telegraphic communication bearing on the situation in Eastern Siberia.
                    It being the desire of my Government to keep you informed of the general line of
                    action which they propose to take on the Siberian situation, I venture to
                    enclose herewith a Memorandum giving a paraphrase of the communication. The
                    information which it contains is not intended for publication, and I shall feel
                    much obliged if you will consider it as confidential.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">K. Shidehara</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d661-a1.xml" xpointer="d661-a1"/>
            </div>
